```text
N_33863(gamma), shape 6022 x 1274,
```

and evaluation reproduces all six root kernels with zero mismatch.

## What Changed

The rank defect, its dimension and its normalized coordinate partition are no
longer observations at a single rational prime. They survive a second
independent completely split algebra, and the complete second-prime relation
coefficients are hash-bound for reconstruction.

This sharply reduces the chance that G3DI observed an exceptional
characteristic. It also supplies the second residue needed to begin rational
reconstruction rather than another support or rank search.

## Boundary

Two finite-prime relation systems still do not prove a relation over
`Q(gamma)`. Their CRT modulus is

```text
21817 * 33863 = 738789071.
```

No coefficient-height bound has yet been proved, and no reconstructed candidate
has yet been checked in the exact polynomial bordered identity. Therefore G3DJ
does not claim

```text
rank_Q(gamma)(Q) = 4748
```

or the characteristic-zero second Woodbury factorization.

The next theorem must add split primes until rational reconstruction is stable
under a held-out prime, then either prove a sufficient height bound or verify
the reconstructed relations directly over `Q(gamma)`.

No Archimedean H02 value, evolving source contraction, coupled path solution,
integral marking, readout or `beta_C` decision is claimed.

